.TH "Docv::Term::Mods" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Term::Mods \- Modifier state; the wire value is \fB\%1 \%+\fR these bits.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBenum Docv::Term::Mods\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Modifier state; the wire value is \fB\%1 \%+\fR these bits.
.SH "ENUM MEMBERS"
.PP
\fBShift = 1_u8\fR
.PP
\fBAlt = 2_u8\fR
.PP
\fBCtrl = 4_u8\fR
.PP
\fBSuper = 8_u8\fR
.PP
\fBHyper = 16_u8\fR
.PP
\fBMeta = 32_u8\fR
.PP
\fBCapsLock = 64_u8\fR
.PP
\fBNumLock = 128_u8\fR
.TP 4
\fBLOCKS = 192_u8\fR
Lock bits are level state, not part of a shortcut.
.TP 4
\fBCOMMAND = 60_u8\fR
Modifiers that make a key a command rather than text.
.PP
\fBNone = 0_u8\fR
.PP
\fBAll = 255_u8\fR
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef normalized : Mods\fR
The modifiers without lock state.
